{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And there shall no longer be</b> a Canaanite — a merchant. The sense is that none of the pots will be sold. And the one who explains a Canaanite literally has no reason, for this family is not known today. And all these passages that are at the end of this book speak of the future. And the one who says that it has already come to pass — let him show me the living waters going out from Jerusalem in summer and in winter."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:47:06.604812616Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}